+# Agent Note: Chat workspace-file open waterfall
+
+Status: implemented
+
+English | [中文](2026-09-05-chat-workspace-file-open-waterfall.zh.md)
+
+## Problem
+
+Chat exposes one `ChatViewInjected.openFile` callback to tool rows, produced-file links, and closing-message mentions. The callback directly invoked the native Host opener, so a Client plugin could not present the file itself without replacing Chat presentation code or adding a second file-open registry.
+
+## Decision
+
+`ChatViewInjected.openFile` dispatches the typed `chat/open-workspace-file` waterfall for file paths. Its request carries the addressed `SessionId` and the workspace path. A listener handles the request by returning without `next()` and delegates by returning `next()`; one request therefore reaches either the handling listener or the terminal native action, never both.
+
+The terminal action preserves the native behavior: it resolves the path with `resolveWorkspacePath(cwd, path)`, calls `session/openWorkspacePath`, and rejects on a Remote refusal. Listener throws and rejections also propagate unchanged to Chat's busy, retry, and stale-settlement handling. The Produced Files **Show in folder** action passes `.` directly to the terminal native action, so directory opening is outside the file waterfall.
+
+The event belongs to ui-chat and names no viewer implementation. An external Client plugin can depend on the exported request type and register an ordinary Cordis listener; ui-chat has no dependency on that plugin.
+
+## Alternatives considered
+
+**Add a file-viewer registry.** Rejected because Cordis already provides ordered, disposable middleware and the Chat callback is the single file-open entry point.
+
+**Always open natively and notify viewers afterward.** Rejected because it double-opens handled files and gives a viewer no way to replace the native action.
+
+**Catch listener failures and fall back to native opening.** Rejected because an unexpected viewer failure would open a second application and hide the failure from Chat's existing retry UI.
+
+## Consequences
+
+Client plugins can replace file opening per request or delegate to the native Host behavior. Focused ui-chat tests pin native fallback, handled short-circuiting, explicit delegation, request identity, error propagation, and the unchanged workspace-folder path. The tool-row file-open decision remains the owner of link presentation and Host opener policy ([tool-call file open](../feature/2026-07-28-tool-call-file-open-in-os.md)).
